wrong[(10, 3) (-4, 1)]: `total > best` keeps the first of the two windows totalling 10: the one starting at index 1.
wrong[(10, 1) (0, -1)]: best starts as None, not 0, so negative totals still count: −4 is the best.
wrong[(9, 0) (-4, 1)]: 7 + 3 = 10 beats 2 + 7 = 9.
