=== task: code hard
title: Different values in every window
prompt: Write `distinct_in_windows(nums, k)` that returns a list with the number of different values in every window of k items, in order. Keep a dictionary of counts and update it as the window slides. The speed check uses long lists with big windows, so building a set for each window is too slow.
starter:
```python
def distinct_in_windows(nums, k):
    counts = {}
    out = []
    # your code here
    return out
```
solution:
```python
def distinct_in_windows(nums, k):
    counts = {}
    out = []
    for right in range(len(nums)):
        x = nums[right]
        counts[x] = counts.get(x, 0) + 1
        if right >= k:
            old = nums[right - k]
            counts[old] -= 1
            if counts[old] == 0:
                del counts[old]
        if right >= k - 1:
            out.append(len(counts))
    return out
```
tests:
